{
  "requirement": "Criteria and their agents should use the SDK's context inspection\noperations for information on which a judgment depends.\nThe context records successful node-content observations in the enclosing\nvalidation's trace. The SDK makes no recording claim for arbitrary filesystem,\nprocess, or network I/O outside that interface. Discovery-only results do not\ncount as full reads of the nodes they locate.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "I derived four obligations from `requirements.sdk.graph.validation-context.tracked_inspection`. The reviewed tests cover each one, and I found no gap. I did not read implementation source or run any searches.\n\n1. **Successful node-content observations are recorded in the enclosing validation's trace.**\n   - `snapshots_record_exact_reads_and_retain_distinct_versions` in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/graph/validation_tests.rs` asserts the exact `Dependency::Node` entries from `read` and `read_snapshot`. It also checks that a later read after a content change adds a distinct entry, and that `finish` copies the same dependencies into the record.\n   - `graph_tools_record_delivered_snapshots_and_prepared_pages_do_not_record_delivery` checks the `read_node` and `get_next_page` tools. Recorded dependencies carry the full 18,000-byte content. Prepared but undelivered inputs are not recorded.\n   - `retries_and_cut_off_tools_preserve_inputs_and_submission_skips_other_reads` checks a single recorded read after retries and cut-off calls.\n   - `concurrent_tool_agents_isolate_histories_pages_and_submissions_and_share_reads` checks the dependencies of two concurrent agents sharing one context.\n   - `source_tools_keep_search_discovery_separate_from_delivered_source_reads` and `cached_selected_source_reads_record_exact_delivered_contents_and_errors_add_no_input` check `read_source`. Each records exactly the provider-supplied observation, with the exact selected content in the cached case.\n   - `domain_shares_discovery_snapshots_with_tracked_reads` in `src/authoring/sdk.rs` checks that a read of the domain's source node records `Dependency::Node` with the delivered fingerprint.\n\n2. **Only successful observations count.**\n   - The snapshot test shows a failed read of node 2 adds no dependency.\n   - The domain test shows a failed read of a missing outline node leaves the dependency count at 1.\n   - `node_preparation_tool_errors_allow_recovery_without_recording_undelivered_contents` and `unknown_tools_return_errors_without_creating_inputs_or_preventing_submission` show tool errors add no dependencies.\n   - The cached source test shows a missing selector adds none.\n   - The graph-tools test and `agent_edge_tools_record_selections_without_validating_targets` show failed deliveries add none.\n\n3. **Discovery-only results do not count as full reads.**\n   - `source_discovery_and_its_pages_do_not_register_reads` runs `list_sources`, `search_text` and `outline_source`, including all of their pages. It asserts empty dependencies on every delivery and zero observation callbacks.\n   - The source-tools test shows `search_text` followed by `read_source` yields exactly one observation.\n   - The cached-source test shows `search_structure` and `outline_source` add nothing. Only the later `read_source` is recorded.\n\n4. **No recording claim for arbitrary I/O, and the SHOULD that criteria use the context operations.** The no-claim text states no behavior that needs testing. The SHOULD is aimed at criteria authors and is exercised by the tests above.",
  "references": "35310360482c2d483323f56fb9de37b8aec413437128e4826fca803225f034fb",
